INT. BELL TOWER OBSERVATION POST - DAWN

A narrow stone chamber under the bells. Sandbags in the arched window. Mist below.

SGT. MBEKI, forties, binoculars up, kneels at the window. PVT. ARNAUD, nineteen, clutches a rifle. CPL. HOSSEINI, thirties, sits against the wall working a field radio. They are silent. He adjusts the dial. He lowers the binoculars. Arnaud's knuckles go white.

MAJOR TULLY (O.S.)
(over radio)
Bell Tower, this is Command. Status report. Over.

MBEKI
(whisper)
Tell him nothing moves.

HOSSEINI
(into radio)
Command, Bell Tower. Nothing moves. Over.

MAJOR TULLY (O.S.)
(over radio)
Keep it that way. Over.

Hosseini sets down the handset. Below, in the fog, something metal clinks. Mbeki holds up a flat hand. Arnaud's rifle trembles. Hosseini slides the radio away from the wall.

ARNAUD
(barely audible)
Sergeant. It's coming from the church.

MBEKI
It's the church that's ours.

A single bell above them swings and sounds, once, deep and sudden.
